decision_rule:
SUPPORTS requires ALL of the following (frozen, no post-hoc weakening):
(1) C1_FULL_BODY_DRIFT: full-vector discrimination >0.5 (expected 1.0 deterministic) on primary same-status body-only comparison STATE_A vs STATE_C (both 200, bodies byte-different, non-CLEN headers identical), with status identity and body SHA inequality and Content-Length difference verified;
(2) C2_BODY_ONLY_SIGNAL: B-BODY-ONLY discrimination >0.5 (expected 1.0) on A vs C and >0.5 on at least one of A vs B per-body isolations; B-HEADERS-NO-CLEN (filtered headers excluding Content-Length) must be 0.0 on A vs C (no independent header drift), while B-HEADERS-ONLY may be 1.0 solely via body-correlated Content-Length (documented, not a failure);
(3) C3_STATUS_ISOLATED: B-STATUS-ONLY =0.0 on A vs C and on A vs B (and on each body-only isolation), proving status confound removed; if >0.0, comparison not same-status and C3 fails;
(4) C4_FULL_EXCEEDS_STATUS_NONVACUOUS: full-vector discrimination > B-STATUS-ONLY strictly on A vs C (e.g., 1.0 > 0.0, complementary to header-only's full 1.0 > max(status 0.0, body 0.0)); equality at ceiling is vacuous and fails this complement test by design, fixing parent V2 for body branch;
(5) C5_NULL_NO_FALSE_POSITIVE: null control N1 (STATE_A resampled, two independent N=20 batches) discrimination_full =0.0 with 95% bootstrap CI containing 0.0 and point estimate <=0.05 (FP<0.05); B-STATUS-ONLY and B-BODY-ONLY also 0.0 on null; exploratory N2 (STATE_C resampled) also 0.0 reported;
(6) C6_CONTENT_LENGTH_VARIES_AND_HEADERS_CONSTANT: Content-Length header values differ across A/B/C proportional to body_len (31 !=52 !=95) and body SHA-256 distinct, while non-Content-Length filtered headers (Cache-Control, ETag, Vary, Set-Cookie) identical across A/B/C, confirming body-only signal not via independent header drift and body semantics differ (fixes Content-Length isolation complement);
(7) C7_WRITABLE_PERMISSION_LEVEL: writable permission-level control discrimination_full >=0.7 (reader body 200 vs admin body 200 via role/content_variant write, same as A vs C, satisfies >=0.7) AND classic permission escalation 403-vs-200 discrimination_full >=0.7 with null FP<0.05 (same-state 403 resampled 0.0) — both verified via committed SQLite role update;
(8) C8_WRITABLE_SESSION_INVALIDATION: writable session-invalidation control discrimination_full >=0.7 on 401-vs-200 (valid session 200 vs DELETE sessions 401) with distinct bodies, and same-state 401 null 0.0 CI contains 0.0 FP<0.05.
If any of C1-C8 fails, verdict = FALSIFIED-IN-SETTING with failing condition(s) identified (body drift not discriminated, isolation violated, null false positive, Content-Length not varying, permission/session below threshold).
If infrastructure prevents verification of status/body/header identity or writable commits (server crash, commit failure, non-200 where 200 required for body-only, body mismatch due to server error), verdict = MEASUREMENT_INVALID with failure category documented. Degenerate bootstrap CI [1.0,1.0]/[0.0,0.0] is EXPECTED and declared valid (not a failure) provided set sizes are 1 and body/header/header-config validity checks pass.
